<title>FINLAND: NOKIA BOUNCES ON ERICSSON H1.</title>
<headline>NOKIA BOUNCES ON ERICSSON H1.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish telecommunications group Nokia bounced on Thursday after its Swedish rival Ericsson reported first-half earnings above analysts' expectations, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1158/0858 GMT, Nokia traded at 455.00 markka, up 30.00 markka or over seven percent, in lively trade.</p>
<p>&quot;It was a really good result ... It's clear that Ericsson and Nokia will rise sharply,&quot; one broker said. Analysts had expected Ericsson to show around 5.11 billion crown profit.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
</text>
